split the string in c#



In C#, you can split a string by using the `String.Split()` method. The method takes a separator (which can be a character or a string) and returns an array of substrings.

Here’s how you could split the string `Please write me a poem about cats` by spaces:
```csharp
string input = "Please write me a poem about cats";
string[] parts = input.Split(' ');

// parts will now be:
// { "Please", "write", "me", "a", "poem", "about", "cats" }
```
You can also use `Split()` with a string:
```csharp
string input = "apple,banana,orange";
string[] fruits = input.Split(',');

// fruits will be { "apple", "banana", "orange" }
```
